    "title": "Reject a suggested action rhetorically",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk3-rhetorical-rejection-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Reject a suggested action rhetorically",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Action + 什么 + 啊 can reject the need for that action. It is a rhetorical, potentially impatient response, not a request for an object.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "看什么啊！",
                "pinyin": "kàn shénme a ！",
                "meaning": "There is no need to look!",
                "audio": "aa82c10ed35b4d04d560fb184b8f1840f972cc17548b0880c5e6a98c72d56680"
              },
              {
                "text": "问什么啊！",
                "pinyin": "wèn shénme a ！",
                "meaning": "There is no need to ask!",
                "audio": "cc83131bd8e13796f586a4919c0fbedf8661bc60618af61564891f563f1be8d9"
